						<main id="main-content" class="asic-page__main">
								<header class="asic-page__header">
									<!-- Page header component goes here -->						
									<h1 class="asic-text-title-large">
										AFS licensee portal access
									</h1>
								</header>							

							<div class="asic-page__article">
								
								<!-- Prose component goes here -->								
<p class="intro">Australian financial services (AFS) licensees must use ASIC’s AFS licensee portal (eLicensing system) to lodge product disclosure statement (PDS) notifications and register managed investment schemes. Many lodgements that were previously made through the AFS licensee portal are now done through the ASIC Regulatory Portal.</p>
<h2>Changes for AFS licensees</h2>
<p>AFS licensees should note:</p>
<ul>
<li>All AFS licence transactions must now be submitted on the ASIC Regulatory Portal. See our <a href="/online-services/asic-portals/asic-regulatory-portal-access" title="Regulatory portal access">Regulatory Portal access page</a>.</li>
<li>Any application or lodgement started but not submitted in the AFS licensee portal before 13 June 2025 must be restarted and submitted in the Regulatory Portal.</li>
<li>AFS licensees must still use the AFS licensee portal to lodge applications to register managed investment schemes and PDS in-use notices. </li>
<li>Credit licence applications and applications relating to registered company auditors must be made using the AFS licensee portal.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Quick links</h2>
<div class="container">
<div class="inside">
<h3>Portal access</h3>
<a href="https://www.edge.asic.gov.au/005/afslportal/get/ServicesLogin" class="asic-button asic-button--primary">Log in</a> <a href="https://www.edge.asic.gov.au/cgi-bin/Lodgement/RC99V004/start/ApplicationLogin" class="asic-button asic-button--secondary">Sign up</a></div>
<div class="inside">
<h3>Support</h3>
<a href="#can" class="asic-button asic-button--secondary" data-anchor="#can">User guides</a></div>
</div>
<h2>Before you start</h2>
<p>You will need an AFS licence name and number to create an account.</p>
<p>If you are not yet an AFS licensee, you will need to apply to become one:</p>
<p class="info-link"><a href="/for-finance-professionals/afs-licensees/applying-for-and-managing-an-afs-licence/faqs-afs-licence-applications/">Information Sheet 294 <em>FAQs: AFS licence applications</em> (INFO 294</a>)</p>
<p>Before signing up, read ASIC’s <a href="/online-services/online-services-information-and-support/electronic-lodgement-protocol" title="Electronic lodgement protocol">Electronic Lodgement Protocol</a>. The protocol includes ASIC’s requirements for storing signed documents that you lodge online.</p>
<!-- ACCORDION START -->
<div class="accordion accordion-expand">
<h2><a name="steps-to-register"></a>Steps to sign up for the AFS licensee portal</h2>
<div class="asic-sequence">
<div class="asic-sequence__section">
<h3 class="asic-sequence__title asic-text-title">Start creating your account</h3>
<ul>
<li>Go to the <a href="https://www.edge.asic.gov.au/cgi-bin/Lodgement/RC99V004/start/ApplicationLogin">sign-up page</a>.</li>
<li>If you agree to the protocol select ‘Yes’. If you do not agree and select ‘No’ you will not be able to sign up.</li>
<li>For the question ‘On what basis are you applying?’, select ‘as an Australian Financial Services licensee’ from the list of options.</li>
<li>Select the ‘Next’ button.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="asic-sequence__section">
<h3 class="asic-sequence__title asic-text-title">Enter your AFS licence number and access</h3>
<ul>
<li>Enter your AFS licence number.</li>
<li>Select the type of documents you are lodging and the access level required. This option allows you to only enter data or to enter data and submit documents.</li>
<li>Select the ‘Next’ button.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="asic-sequence__section">
<h3 class="asic-sequence__title asic-text-title">Enter username, password and security question and answer</h3>
<ul>
<li>Make your username something easy to remember.</li>
<li>Your password must:
<ul>
<li>be 16 to 50 characters long</li>
<li>include at least one lowercase letter (a–z), one capital letter (A–Z) and one number (0–9).</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>For your security question, choose something you will remember the answer to. If you lose your password and forget the answer to your security question, you’ll need to create a new account.</li>
<li>Enter all details and select the ‘Next’ button. A popup box will appear. Enter your username and password again, then select the ‘Next’ button.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="asic-sequence__section">
<h3 class="asic-sequence__title asic-text-title">Enter contact email address and phone number</h3>
<ul>
<li>Once you create an online account, ASIC will send correspondence about your licence to an online inbox. When you have a new inbox message, we’ll send an email to the address you enter here, so make it an address you check often.</li>
<li>Enter your email address and phone number, then select the ‘Next’ button.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="asic-sequence__section">
<h3 class="asic-sequence__title asic-text-title">Print, sign and send</h3>
<p>You will need to print and sign a participation agreement and email it to <a href="mailto:agent.registration@asic.gov.au">agent.registration@asic.gov.au</a>. Once you have submitted the agreement, select ‘Yes’ and then ‘Next’.</p>
</div>
<div class="asic-sequence__section">
<h3 class="asic-sequence__title asic-text-title">Declare and submit</h3>
<ul>
<li>Fill in the declaration details, then select the ‘Submit’ button.</li>
<li>You’ll see a screen confirming your request has been submitted.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="asic-sequence__section">
<h3 class="asic-sequence__title asic-text-title">Activate your online access account</h3>
<p>ASIC will contact you within 2 business days to confirm your account has been activated.</p>
</div>
</div>
<!-- SEQUENCE END --></div>
<h2><a id="can"></a><a id="user-guides"></a>What you can do using the AFS licensee portal</h2>
<p>You can do the following tasks on the AFS licensee portal. Select a heading to see user guides and links for each task.</p>
<!-- ACCORDION START -->
<div class="accordion">
<h3>Lodge PDS notifications</h3>
<h4>User guide</h4>
<p><a href="https://download.asic.gov.au/media/1348310/Userguide_AFSL_FS88_89_90.pdf">Lodging PDS notifications online: A user guide for AFS licensees (PDF 1.2 MB)</a></p>
<h3>Register a managed investment scheme</h3>
<h4>User guide</h4>
<p><a href="https://download.asic.gov.au/media/1192298/user-guide-afsl-5100a.pdf">How to lodge an application for registration of a managed investment scheme: A user guide for AFS licensees (PDF 358 KB)</a></p>
</div>
<h2><a id="cannot"></a>What you cannot do using the AFS licensee portal</h2>
<p>You cannot do the following tasks on the AFS licensee portal. Select a heading to see more information.</p>
<!-- ACCORDION START -->
<div class="accordion">
<h3>Tasks now done through the ASIC Regulatory Portal</h3>
<p>Many tasks and lodgements previously done through the AFS licensee portal are now done through the <a href="/online-services/asic-portals/asic-regulatory-portal-access" title="Regulatory portal access">Regulatory Portal</a>.</p>
<p>These include:</p>
<ul>
<li>applying for an AFS licence</li>
<li>changing your AFS licence information</li>
<li>appointing an auditor</li>
<li>varying or cancelling licence authorisations and conditions</li>
<li>lodging annual accounts and audit reports</li>
<li>notifying ASIC of a change in control of an AFS licensee</li>
<li>changing responsible managers.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Appoint or update an authorised representative or a financial adviser</h3>
<p>To appoint or update an authorised representative or a financial adviser, you will need to use another system called ASIC Connect:</p>
<p><a href="/online-services/asic-portals/afs-licensee-portal-access/appoint-or-update-an-authorised-representative-or-financial-adviser" title="Financial advisers and authorised representatives">Appoint or update an authorised representative or a financial adviser</a></p>
</div>									


							</div>

							
						</main>

